  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Glucagon is a pancreatic hormone used to treat severe low blood sugar in people with diabetes. It is an approved medicine, listed among WHO essential medicines, and products are authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q170617&quot;>Wikidata Q170617</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>glucagon</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>H04AA01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00040&quot;>DB00040</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/154724000&quot;>154724000</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q170617&quot;>Q170617</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C153H229Cl4N43O49S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>3628.63 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
